 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? Take a deep breath. Think of what you actually want, not what you always order. How does it look after you' tried it? Ask if the chef has a favourite. Order that. They know it best and are excited to show it off. It is. chefs love it when someone appreciates their favourite. Ask at the table, not when you' still full. Sometimes. Check the date. If it' months old, ask for something fresh instead. If they keep bad stock, don't come back. Because people are sometimes mean and groans start rumors. Keep it to yourself.",
